      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHO IS ALAN (10) has been hard to fault of late and he made it two in a row when successful at his latest appearance over 1740m at Riverina Paceway, getting home by 4 metres. Hard to know where he gets from this slightly awkward draw. Taking on a better field but he is capable of running another bold race. HOLY CAMP DILLON (6) finished fifth last start over 2260m at Bathurst, beaten 15 metres, after a modest seventh at Bathurst the run prior. Meets a similar quality field and is good enough to put himself in the winners' stall. JEKAMIAS NZ (7) is better than his last-start run for eighth over 1740m at Riverina Paceway would suggest. Each-way. RUDIMENTARY (9) disappointed last time as the favourite when ninth over 2260m at Bathurst. Can do a lot better so is worth considering.",
